<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Nucleus-MoE Diffusers Implementation Guide</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light dark;
      --bg: #f7f8fb;
      --ink: #16181d;
      --muted: #586174;
      --panel: #ffffff;
      --panel-2: #eef2f7;
      --line: #d9e0ea;
      --accent: #0f766e;
      --accent-2: #7c2d12;
      --code: #101828;
      --code-bg: #e8edf5;
    }

    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root {
        --bg: #101318;
        --ink: #edf1f7;
        --muted: #a8b1c3;
        --panel: #171b22;
        --panel-2: #202631;
        --line: #303846;
        --accent: #5eead4;
        --accent-2: #fdba74;
        --code: #f8fafc;
        --code-bg: #111827;
      }
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    main {
      max-width: 1120px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 32px 20px 56px;
    }

    header {
      padding: 28px 0 18px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 34px 0 12px;
      font-size: 1.55rem;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    h3 {
      margin: 24px 0 10px;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    p {
      margin: 10px 0;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .lede {
      max-width: 820px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 1.08rem;
    }

    .meta {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 8px;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    .pill {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      background: var(--panel);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 14px;
      margin: 18px 0;
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 16px;
    }

    .card strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
    }

    .warn {
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-2);
    }

    .ok {
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    }

    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 14px 0 22px;
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    th,
    td {
      padding: 10px 12px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      text-align: left;
      vertical-align: top;
    }

    th {
      background: var(--panel-2);
    }

    code {
      color: var(--code);
      background: var(--code-bg);
      border-radius: 4px;
      padding: 1px 5px;
      font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
      font-size: 0.95em;
    }

    pre {
      overflow: auto;
      background: var(--code-bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 14px;
    }

    pre code {
      padding: 0;
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--code);
    }

    ol,
    ul {
      padding-left: 1.3rem;
    }

    li {
      margin: 7px 0;
    }

    .toc {
      columns: 2;
      column-gap: 32px;
      margin: 18px 0;
    }

    .toc a {
      display: block;
      break-inside: avoid;
      margin: 5px 0;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    @media (max-width: 820px) {
      .grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .toc {
        columns: 1;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <header>
      <h1>Nucleus-MoE Diffusers Implementation Guide</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A companion guide for adding Nucleus-MoE, published as
        <code>NucleusAI/Nucleus-Image</code>, to SynthaEngine without hiding the
        memory reality of a 17B sparse MoE image model on an RTX 3060 12 GB.
      </p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span class="pill">Date: 2026-05-30</span>
        <span class="pill">Target PC: 64 GB RAM, RTX 3060 12 GB</span>
        <span class="pill">Diffusers: 0.38.0 verified locally</span>
        <span class="pill">Task: text-to-image</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="toc">
      <h2 id="toc">Contents</h2>
      <nav class="toc">
        <a href="#summary">1. Executive Summary</a>
        <a href="#what">2. What Nucleus-MoE Is</a>
        <a href="#support">3. Diffusers Support</a>
        <a href="#hardware">4. Hardware Fit</a>
        <a href="#smoke">5. Smoke Test</a>
        <a href="#method">6. New Pipeline Method</a>
        <a href="#implementation">7. SynthaEngine Plan</a>
        <a href="#hosted">8. Hosted Provider Path</a>
        <a href="#risks">9. Risks</a>
        <a href="#done">10. Definition of Done</a>
        <a href="#sources">11. Sources</a>
      </nav>
    </section>

    <section id="summary">
      <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card ok">
          <strong>Pipeline exists locally</strong>
          <p>
            The repo venv imports <code>NucleusMoEImagePipeline</code>,
            <code>NucleusMoEImageTransformer2DModel</code>, and
            <code>TextKVCacheConfig</code> with Diffusers 0.38.0.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card warn">
          <strong>12 GB VRAM is not enough for direct BF16</strong>
          <p>
            The Hub tree reports about 51.7 GB of model files. The transformer
            alone is about 33.8 GB and the text encoder is about 17.5 GB.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <strong>Recommended status</strong>
          <p>
            Treat local Nucleus-MoE as experimental. Use a standalone smoke
            test, one-shot subprocesses, one image per job, low defaults, and
            CPU offload.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p>
        Nucleus-MoE activates only about 2B of its 17B parameters per forward
        pass, which improves compute efficiency. It does not remove the need to
        store, load, offload, or stream the full model stack.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="what">
      <h2>2. What Nucleus-MoE Is</h2>
      <p>
        Nucleus-MoE, published as <code>NucleusAI/Nucleus-Image</code>, is a
        text-to-image sparse Mixture-of-Experts diffusion transformer. The
        older name <code>NucleusAI/NucleusMoE-Image</code> redirects to the
        current repository.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Total parameters</td><td>17B</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Active parameters</td><td>About 2B</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Architecture</td><td>Sparse MoE diffusion transformer</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Layers</td><td>32</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Experts per MoE layer</td><td>64 routed experts plus 1 shared expert</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Text encoder</td><td>Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Image tokenizer</td><td>Qwen-Image VAE</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Scheduler</td><td>FlowMatch Euler discrete scheduler</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="support">
      <h2>3. Diffusers Support</h2>
      <p>
        Diffusers documents <code>NucleusMoEImagePipeline</code> as a pipeline
        with a Nucleus MoE transformer, FlowMatch Euler scheduler,
        Qwen3-VL processor and text encoder, and Qwen-Image VAE. The local
        SynthaEngine venv already exposes the pipeline.
      </p>
      <pre><code>.venv\Scripts\python.exe -c "import diffusers; print(diffusers.__version__); print(hasattr(diffusers, 'NucleusMoEImagePipeline'))"</code></pre>
      <pre><code>0.38.0
True</code></pre>
      <p>
        The official quick start uses <code>DiffusionPipeline.from_pretrained</code>
        and then <code>pipe.to("cuda")</code>. For this PC, the implementation
        should not do that by default.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="hardware">
      <h2>4. Hardware Fit</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Mode</th><th>Expected Result</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Official BF16 with <code>pipe.to("cuda")</code></td>
            <td>Not viable on 12 GB VRAM</td>
            <td>Avoid</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>BF16 with model CPU offload</td>
            <td>May load, likely slow, RAM tight</td>
            <td>Smoke test only</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>BF16 with sequential CPU offload</td>
            <td>Safer for VRAM, very slow</td>
            <td>Best local experiment</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Generic quantization</td>
            <td>Uncertain for MoE expert tensors</td>
            <td>Validate before exposing</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Hosted fal provider</td>
            <td>Practical now</td>
            <td>Best reliable path</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="smoke">
      <h2>5. Smoke Test</h2>
      <p>
        Before any application integration, run a standalone script with one
        prompt, one image, 512x512 resolution, 8 steps, BF16, Text KV cache,
        VAE slicing/tiling, and sequential CPU offload.
      </p>
      <pre><code>import torch
from diffusers import DiffusionPipeline, TextKVCacheConfig

pipe = DiffusionPipeline.from_pretrained(
    "NucleusAI/Nucleus-Image",
    torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16,
)

if hasattr(pipe.transformer, "enable_cache"):
    pipe.transformer.enable_cache(TextKVCacheConfig())

if getattr(pipe, "vae", None) is not None:
    pipe.vae.enable_slicing()
    pipe.vae.enable_tiling()

pipe.enable_sequential_cpu_offload()

image = pipe(
    prompt="a clean product photo of a matte black ceramic mug on a walnut desk",
    width=512,
    height=512,
    num_inference_steps=8,
    guidance_scale=4.0,
    generator=torch.Generator(device="cpu").manual_seed(42),
).images[0]
image.save("nucleus_moe_smoke.png")</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section id="method">
      <h2>6. New Pipeline Method</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Confirm the official model card, Diffusers docs, and <code>model_index.json</code>.</li>
        <li>Verify local imports with the repo venv.</li>
        <li>Classify the task and choose a stable public task identifier.</li>
        <li>Estimate memory from Hub file sizes before writing code.</li>
        <li>Create a standalone smoke test.</li>
        <li>Design minimal workflow schema and output shape.</li>
        <li>Implement runtime in a family package, preferably subprocess-backed.</li>
        <li>Register schema, handler, and catalog capabilities.</li>
        <li>Update docs and tests together.</li>
        <li>Add a frontend page only after backend behavior is proven.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="implementation">
      <h2>7. SynthaEngine Plan</h2>
      <h3>Family and Task</h3>
      <pre><code>family: nucleus-moe
aliases: nucleus-image, nucleusmoe, nucleus
task: nucleus-moe.text2img</code></pre>

      <h3>Future Files</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><code>backend/workflow/nucleus_moe.py</code></li>
        <li><code>backend/nucleus_moe/__init__.py</code></li>
        <li><code>backend/nucleus_moe/pipeline.py</code></li>
        <li><code>backend/nucleus_moe/subprocess_runner.py</code></li>
        <li><code>frontend/nucleus_moe/text2img.html</code> after backend proof</li>
        <li><code>frontend/nucleus_moe/text2img.js</code> after backend proof</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Initial Input Defaults</h3>
      <pre><code>{
  "steps": 8,
  "guidance_scale": 4.0,
  "width": 512,
  "height": 512,
  "num_images": 1,
  "memory_preset": "sequential_offload",
  "enable_text_kv_cache": true,
  "experimental_ack": true
}</code></pre>

      <h3>Workflow Example</h3>
      <pre><code>{
  "kind": "workflow",
  "payload": {
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "t1",
        "type": "nucleus-moe.text2img",
        "inputs": {
          "prompt": "a quiet alpine lake at sunrise, soft pink and gold sky",
          "width": 512,
          "height": 512,
          "steps": 8,
          "guidance_scale": 4.0,
          "memory_preset": "sequential_offload",
          "experimental_ack": true
        }
      }
    ],
    "return": "@t1.images"
  }
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section id="hosted">
      <h2>8. Hosted Provider Path</h2>
      <p>
        If the goal is reliable Nucleus output on this PC, a hosted provider is
        more practical than local BF16. A hosted path should be a separate
        approved behavior change because it introduces credentials, remote
        execution, and output download handling.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="risks">
      <h2>9. Risks</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Risk</th><th>Mitigation</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Huge model download and cache footprint</td><td>Document disk needs and require smoke test.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Out-of-memory on 12 GB VRAM</td><td>Never default to direct CUDA loading.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>64 GB RAM still tight</td><td>Use one-shot subprocesses and one image per job.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sequential offload is slow</td><td>Mark local mode experimental.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Generic quantization may miss MoE tensors</td><td>Validate real peak memory before exposing it.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section id="done">
      <h2>10. Definition of Done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Standalone smoke test completes or feature is explicitly hosted-only.</li>
        <li><code>nucleus-moe.text2img</code> appears in task type discovery.</li>
        <li>Catalog includes <code>nucleus-moe</code> capabilities.</li>
        <li>Workflow job returns <code>{ "images": ["/outputs/..."] }</code>.</li>
        <li>Runtime is subprocess-backed and cleans up memory in <code>finally</code>.</li>
        <li>Docs and mocked tests are updated without downloading the real model.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="sources">
      <h2>11. Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://huggingface.co/NucleusAI/Nucleus-Image">NucleusAI/Nucleus-Image model card</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://huggingface.co/NucleusAI/Nucleus-Image/tree/main">NucleusAI/Nucleus-Image file tree</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/diffusers/main/api/pipelines/nucleusmoe_image">Diffusers NucleusMoE pipeline docs</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/diffusers/using-diffusers/loading">Diffusers pipeline loading docs</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/diffusers/main/en/optimization/memory">Diffusers memory reduction docs</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/diffusers/main/quantization/overview">Diffusers quantization overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12163">Nucleus-Image arXiv paper</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
